        "@value": "Structure Type"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf": [
      {
        "@id": "_:n908fb06c9e6143c3be2ae96a746557e3b175"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type"
      },
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A type of heritage structure from a controlled vocabulary or a community's own term list (a CIDOC-CRM E55 Type), e.g. the Newar bahah or bahi (Buddhist monastic courtyard), dyochhen (god-house), agam chhen (esoteric shrine house) or pitha (seat of a goddess). Link each term to AAT or Wikidata with SKOS mappings where an equivalent exists; local types need no new ontology class."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/schema"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:n908fb06c9e6143c3be2ae96a746557e3b175",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#allValuesFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P3_has_note"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P129_is_about",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "is about"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Quantification: many to many (0,n:0,n)\n\nScope note:\nThis property documents that an instance of E89 Propositional Object has as subject an instance of E1 CRM Entity. \nThis differs from P67 refers to (is referred to by), which refers to an instance of E1 CRM Entity, in that it describes the primary subject or subjects of an instance of E89 Propositional Object.\n\nExamples:\n- The text entitled ‘Reach for the sky’ (E33) is about Douglas Bader (E21). (Brickhill, 2001)\n\nIn First Order Logic:\n- P129(x,y) ⇒ E89(x)\n- P129(x,y) ⇒ E1(y) \n- P129(x,y) ⇒ P67(x,y)"
      }
    ]
  },
