  {
    "@id": "https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/confidenceMethod",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/extensions/crminf/I2_Belief"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/ontology"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Confidence method"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E29_Design_or_Procedure"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The documented procedure (crm:E29 Design or Procedure) by which the confidence score was assigned, described once (e.g. an expert 5-point scale mapped to 0-1, agreement between independent sources, or coding of the source's hedging: 0.9 stated plainly, 0.7 mild hedging, 0.5 explicitly uncertain, 0.3 disputed by the author)."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/schema"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P14i_performed",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "performed"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Quantification of the inverse property: many to many, necessary (1,n:0,n)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property describes the active participation of an instance of E39 Actor in an instance of E7 Activity. \nIt implies causal or legal responsibility. The P14.1 in the role of property of the property specifies the nature of an Actor’s participation.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The painting of the Sistine Chapel (E7) carried out by Michelangelo Buonaroti (E21) in the role of master craftsman (E55). (Goldscheider, 1953)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P14(x,y) ⇒ E7(x)\n- P14(x,y)⇒ E39(y)\n- P14(x,y) ⇒ P11(x,y)\n- P14(x,y,z) ⇒ [P14(x,y) ∧ E55(z)]"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o#"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "Activity"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@value": "An activity is something that occurs over a period of time and acts upon or with entities; it may include consuming, processing, transforming, modifying, relocating, using, or generating entities."
      }
    ]
  },
