    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Buddhist votive shrine (chaitya); votive stupa form found across the Kathmandu Valley. In Newar usage chaitya (Newar chibhah) also names great stupas (Swayambhu Mahachaitya), so a monument may be both a Stupa and a Chaitya."
      }
    ],
