  {
    "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P4_has_time-span",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "has time-span"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Quantification: many to one, necessary (1,1:0,n)\n\nScope note:\nThis property associates an instance of E2 Temporal Entity with the instance of E52 Time-Span during which it was on-going. The associated instance of E52 Time-Span is understood as the real time-span during which the phenomena making up the temporal entity instance were active. More than one instance of E2 Temporal Entity may share a common instance of E52 Time-Span only if they come into being and end being due to identical declarations or events.\n\nExamples:\n- The Yalta Conference (E7) has time-span Yalta Conference time-span (E52). (Harbutt, 2010)\n\nIn First Order Logic:\n- P4(x,y) ⇒ E2(x)\n- P4(x,y) ⇒ E52(y)"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P98i_was_born",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "was born"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Quantification of the inverse property: one to many, dependent (0,n:1,1)\n\nScope note of the inverse property:\nThis property links an instance of E67 Birth event to an instance of E21 Person in the role of offspring.\nTwins, triplets etc. are brought into life by the same instance of E67 Birth. This is not intended for use with general Natural History material, only people. There is no explicit method for modelling conception and gestation except by using extensions.\n\nExamples of the inverse property:\n- The Birth of Queen Elizabeth II (E67) brought into life Queen Elizabeth II (E21). (Parker, 2002)\n\nIn First Order Logic of the inverse property:\n- P98(x,y) ⇒ E67(x)\n- P98(x,y) ⇒ E21(y)\n- P98(x,y) ⇒ P92(x,y)"
      }
    ]
  },
